<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Slovenia</h1><p class="st-meta">1991 CE – present · capital Ljubljana</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Central European republic that declared independence from Yugoslavia on 25 June 1991 after the Ten-Day War, and joined the EU and NATO in 2004.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Slovenia declared independence on 25 June 1991, having been one of six republics of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/socialist-federal-republic-of-yugoslavia">Socialist Federal Republic of Yugoslavia</a>. More than 88% of voters had backed independence on 23 December 1990. The Yugoslav People's Army moved against the declaration, which led to the Ten-Day War, and the Brioni Agreement of 7 July brought a truce. The last Yugoslav soldiers left at the end of July.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parliamentary-democracy">Parliamentary democracy</a> had been introduced in September 1989, and the first democratic election in April 1990 was won by the opposition movement DEMOS under Jože Pučnik. A new constitution was adopted in December 1991. From 1992 to 2004 the Liberal Democracy of Slovenia governed and moved the economy gradually from the Titoist model to a market economy; Janez Drnovšek was prime minister from 1992 to 2002 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> Kučan president from 1990 to 2002. Slovenia joined the EU and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> in 2004 and the eurozone on 1 January 2007.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Slovenia is a parliamentary republic with a multi-party system and a president elected by popular vote for five years. Janez Janša became prime minister for a third time in March 2020. On 22 May 2026 the National Assembly appointed him prime minister for a fourth time, backed by 51 of 87 deputies.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/slovenia.jpg" alt="Slovenia" width="330" height="165"><figcaption>Image: Original: Marko Pogačnik Vector: Achim1999 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Slovenia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1991 CE – pres